  "question": {
    "text": "A horizontal metallic rod of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> is supported by two vertical identical springs of spring constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;each and natural length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. A current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi></math>&nbsp;is flowing in the rod in the direction shown. If the rod is in equilibrium then the length of each spring in this state is:<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0039_debaa5b455df.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 73px;\" />\r"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">ilB</mtext><mo>-</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">mg</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>K</mi></mfrac></math>",
